//MCQ

::Bigdata Introduction::
Unprocessed data or processed data are observations or measurements that can be expressed as text, numbers, or other types of media.
{T}

::Bigdata Introduction::
Which is a symbolic representation of facts or concepts from which information may be obtained with a reasonable degree of confidence?
{
=Data
~Knowledge
~Analysis
~Algorithm
}

::Bigdata Introduction::
In Big Data environments, Velocity refers
{
~Data can arrive at fast speed
~Enormous datasets can accumulate within very short periods of time
~Velocity of data translates into the amount of time it takes for the data to be processed
=All of the mentioned above
}

::Bigdata Introduction::
State True/False - Structured data conforms to a data schema and is often stored in tabular form.
{T}

::Bigdata Introduction::
which of the following is an example of unstructured data?
{
~Students roll number, age
~Videos
~Audio files
=Both B and C
}


